@startuml
title Order standing transfer
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow false
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
actor "Customer" as customer
participant "Customer Web App\n(React SPA)" as spa
participant "Core Banking API\n(FastAPI)" as api
database "PostgreSQL" as db

customer -> spa : On Scheduled Transfers fills in: source account, recipient account number (IBAN), amount, description, frequency, start date
spa -> spa : Validates the form (required fields, amount > 0, start date >= today)
spa -> api : POST /scheduled-transactions {sourceAccountId, recipientAccountNumber, amount, description, frequency, startDate}
api -> api : Authenticates the user (token)

alt invalid or missing token
    api --> spa : 401 Unauthorized
    spa --> customer : Redirects to login
else authenticated
    api -> api : Validates the payload (amount > 0, IBAN format, frequency in {WEEKLY, MONTHLY, ...}, startDate >= today)
    alt invalid payload
        api --> spa : 422 validation error
        spa --> customer : Shows validation errors
    else payload valid
        api -> db : SELECT id, user_id, status, currency_code FROM accounts\nWHERE id = :sourceAccountId OR account_number = :recipientAccountNumber
        db --> api : account rows
        alt source not owned by user
            api --> spa : 403 Forbidden
            spa --> customer : Shows error message
        else recipient not found
            api --> spa : 404 Not Found
            spa --> customer : Shows error message
        else account not ACTIVE / source = recipient
            api --> spa : 422 Unprocessable Entity
            spa --> customer : Shows error message
        else data is valid
            api -> api : Maps frequency + startDate to cron_expression (Europe/Warsaw),\ne.g. MONTHLY from the 10th -> '0 0 10 * *'
            api -> api : Computes next_run_at = first occurrence >= startDate, converted to UTC
            api -> db : INSERT INTO scheduled_transactions (id = uuid4(), source_account_id, target_account_id,\ncurrency = source.currency_code, amount, description, cron_expression, next_run_at, status = 'ACTIVE')
            db --> api : inserted
            api --> spa : 201 Created {id, nextRunAt, status: "ACTIVE"}
            spa --> customer : Shows the new entry on the Scheduled Transfers list
        end
    end
end

note over api, db
No balance check at creation time - funds and (if needed) the exchange rate
are evaluated when the transfer is executed. The order runs until the customer
cancels it (status = 'CANCELLED'). Executed by the Scheduled Job Worker (separate flow).
end note
@enduml
